==Portuguese==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|pt|roa-opt|monte}}, from {{inh|pt|la|montem}}, accusative of {{m|la|mōns}}, from {{der|pt|ine-pro|*men-||mountain}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|PT}} {{IPA|pt|/ˈmõ.tɨ/}}
* {{a|BR}} {{IPA|pt|/ˈmõ.t͡ʃi/}}
** {{a|Northeast Brazil}} {{IPA|pt|[ˈmõ.tɪ]|[ˈmõ.tʲ]}}
** {{a|South Brazil}} {{IPA|pt|/ˈmõ.te/|[ˈmõ.te]|[ˈmõ.tɪ]}}
* {{hyphenation|pt|mon|te}}

===Noun===
{{pt-noun|m}}

# {{l|en|mount}}; a {{l|en|mountain}} or large {{l|en|hill}}
#: {{syn|pt|[[montanha]] {{q|mountain}}|[[morro]] {{q|large hill}}}}
# {{l|en|pile}}; {{l|en|heap}} {{gloss|a mass of things placed together so as to form a mass or elevation}}
#: {{syn|pt|pilha|amontoado}}
# {{lb|pt|usually in {{l|pt|um monte de|gloss=a lot of}}}} {{l|en|heap}}; {{l|en|load}}; {{l|en|pile}} {{gloss|a great amount of something}}
#: {{ux|pt|Eu conheco um '''monte''' de gente.|I know a '''lot of''' people.|inline=1}}
#: {{syn|pt|amontoado|pilha|penca}}
# {{lb|pt|inheritance law}} a share of personal property given to someone as part of an {{l|en|inheritance}}, or the property as a whole; {{l|en|legacy}}
# {{lb|pt|Alentejo}} a rural property or group of farm buildings

====Usage notes====
''Monte'' is usually used in reference to elevations smaller than {{l|pt|montanha|montanhas|mountains}}. However, ''monte'' (and not ''montanha'') is used in the full title of mountains regardless of size: ''Monte Everest'', ''Monte Aconcágua''.

